From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libvmaf: map percentile pool methods on the vmaf filters

VMAFx libvmaf (ADR-1188) appends MEDIAN / PERC5 / PERC10 / PERC20 to
VmafPoolingMethod, and defines VMAF_HAVE_PERCENTILE_POOLING when they are
available. Map the matching pool= option strings so every vmaf filter
variant (libvmaf, libvmaf_cuda, libvmaf_sycl, libvmaf_metal, ...) can
report the "worst 10% of frames" summary the Python harness has always
offered. Also map "max", which the enum has always had but the mapper
never accepted. Unknown strings still fall back to mean.

The percentile block is guarded by the feature macro so the filter still
builds against an upstream Netflix libvmaf.
---
 doc/filters.texi         |  6 +++++-
 libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/filters.texi b/doc/filters.texi
index 3534c87..489bd7e 100644
--- a/doc/filters.texi
+++ b/doc/filters.texi
@@ -17470,7 +17470,11 @@ Set the format of the log file (xml, json, csv, or sub).
 
 @item pool
 Set the pool method to be used for computing vmaf.
-Options are @code{min}, @code{harmonic_mean} or @code{mean} (default).
+Options are @code{min}, @code{max}, @code{harmonic_mean} or @code{mean}
+(default). When built against a libvmaf that provides the order-statistic
+pooling methods (VMAFx >= 3.2), @code{median}, @code{perc5}, @code{perc10} and
+@code{perc20} select the corresponding percentile of the per-frame scores,
+interpolated linearly between ranks.
 
 @item n_threads
 Set number of threads to be used when initializing libvmaf.
diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c b/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
index 4ff00c6..ef28a74 100644
--- a/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
@@ -940,13 +940,30 @@ static enum VmafOutputFormat log_fmt_map(const char *log_fmt)
 
 static enum VmafPoolingMethod pool_method_map(const char *pool_method)
 {
+    /* libvmaf >= 3.2 (fork ADR-1188) additionally exposes the order-statistic
+     * methods; "max" has always existed in the enum but was never mapped. The
+     * strings match the Python harness spellings so a pool= option means the
+     * same thing on both surfaces. Unknown strings keep falling back to mean,
+     * as upstream. */
     if (pool_method) {
         if (!strcmp(pool_method, "min"))
             return VMAF_POOL_METHOD_MIN;
+        if (!strcmp(pool_method, "max"))
+            return VMAF_POOL_METHOD_MAX;
         if (!strcmp(pool_method, "mean"))
             return VMAF_POOL_METHOD_MEAN;
         if (!strcmp(pool_method, "harmonic_mean"))
             return VMAF_POOL_METHOD_HARMONIC_MEAN;
+#ifdef VMAF_HAVE_PERCENTILE_POOLING
+        if (!strcmp(pool_method, "median"))
+            return VMAF_POOL_METHOD_MEDIAN;
+        if (!strcmp(pool_method, "perc5"))
+            return VMAF_POOL_METHOD_PERC5;
+        if (!strcmp(pool_method, "perc10"))
+            return VMAF_POOL_METHOD_PERC10;
+        if (!strcmp(pool_method, "perc20"))
+            return VMAF_POOL_METHOD_PERC20;
+#endif
     }
 
     return VMAF_POOL_METHOD_MEAN;
